  "status": "STATICALLY_REJECTED",
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "question": "Can the project's R580 UVM bridge safely serve one R580 nvidia-uvm consumer across separately initialized R580 Open and R580 proprietary backends?",
  "decision_summary": "No, statically. In non-Confidential-Computing mode (always on Volta) the pinned public R580 consumer adds a GPU only after mapping every already-registered GPU's sysmem semaphore pool into it with nvUvmInterfaceDupAllocation(owner VA space, new GPU VA space). No route exists for a pair spanning two RM providers; the bridge correctly rejects it with NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED before either RM is called. One UVM instance therefore cannot hold GPUs of both providers at once. Callback registration, rollback and ownership routing are internally consistent and fail-closed for one provider at a time.",
  "smallest_blocker": {
    "id": "C1",
    "missing_contract": "A cross-provider DupAllocation: making one RM's sysmem allocation addressable in the other RM's GPU VA space, with coherent cross-GPU semaphore acquires.",
